msm is the Linux DRM driver for Qualcomm Adreno GPUs, built as a FreeBSD
kernel module against drm-kmod.  It attaches to the GPU the firmware's
ACPI tables describe, and is loaded at boot by devmatch(8).  It provides
the render node that Mesa's freedreno (OpenGL) and Turnip (Vulkan)
drivers use; it does not drive displays.

Supported: SC8280XP (Snapdragon 8cx Gen 3, Adreno 690).
